# UI copy grammar

When Nephi suggests UI copy (messages, labels, notices, tooltips) that is grammatically incorrect, use the corrected wording and tell him afterwards what changed and why, in one short line. Examples: hyphenate compound modifiers before a noun ("System-locked records"), and split comma splices into two sentences ("Record is locked. Contact your admin to unlock it.").

Apply the same check to copy already in the product when touching it.
